---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BootChain from '../components/BootChain.astro';
import Status from '../components/Status.astro';
import { checkedOn } from '../data/boot-chain';

const checked = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', { dateStyle: 'long', timeZone: 'UTC' }).format(
  new Date(`${checkedOn}T00:00:00Z`),
);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Kyro: open-source PXE server for Windows 11"
  description="Kyro is an open-source PXE server for installing Windows 11 over the network. It is in early development and cannot boot a machine yet."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Kyro is an open-source PXE server for installing Windows&nbsp;11 over the network.</h1>
    <Status state="in-progress" block>
      Kyro is being designed and cannot boot a machine yet. This page says so until that changes.
    </Status>
    <p>
      The goal: you point Kyro at a Windows 11 ISO, and a PC that boots from the network gets
      Windows Setup from it. No USB stick, no unpacking the ISO by hand, and with an answer file
      no one has to sit in front of the installer.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="chain">
    <h2 id="chain">From power-on to Windows Setup</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Six things have to happen before Windows Setup runs on a machine that booted from the
      network. Kyro is meant to serve all of them from one program.
    </p>
    <BootChain />
    <p class="note chain-note">
      Compared with the{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/kyro-pxe/kyro/blob/main/docs/ROADMAP.md">roadmap in the Kyro repository</a>{' '}
      on {checked}. If the two differ, the roadmap is right.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="split">
    <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="generator">
      <h2 id="generator">Answer file generator</h2>
      <p>
        <Status state="planned">The options are written down as a proposal. Nothing is built.</Status>
      </p>
      <p>
        A form on this site is going to create <code>autounattend.xml</code> files: language,
        accounts, disk layout and the other things Windows Setup would otherwise ask. It is
        meant to run in the browser only, so that what you type, passwords included, stays on
        your computer.
      </p>
      <ul class="links">
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/kyro-pxe/website/blob/main/docs/adr/0001-generator-options.md">Read the proposed option set</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="project">
      <h2 id="project">Project</h2>
      <ul class="links">
        <li><a href="https://github.com/kyro-pxe/kyro">Kyro source code</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/kyro-pxe/kyro/blob/main/docs/ROADMAP.md">Roadmap</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/kyro-pxe/kyro/blob/main/docs/security-model.md">Security model</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/kyro-pxe/website">Source of this site</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .chain-note {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }
</style>
